express cookie
    -small files/data(store user detail or login credetial like username, user id etc,) that are sent to client with a server request and stored on the client side, so that user don' have to login next time in that site (if cookie is stores or not destroyed) .
    -every time the user loads webiste back, this cookie is sent back with the request to the server so that server know the user.

    The following are the numerous uses of the HTTP Cookies −
        -Session management
        -Personalization(Recommendation systems)
        -User tracking

    to use cookie with express install this:
        npm install --save cookie-parser 
        (you can write i instate of install and -- save is optional)

        Now to use cookies with Express, we will require the cookie-parser. cookie-parser is a middleware which parses cookies attached to the client request object.

        cookie-parser parses Cookie header and populates req.cookies with an object keyed by the cookie names.

        -adding cookie with expire time
            - two way
                -expire property -just pass an object with property 'expire' set to the time when you want it to expire
                - maxAge promerty: Using this property, we can provide relative time instead of absolute time

        - deleting existing cookie
            To delete a cookie, use the clearCookie function.




express session
    - A session is a way to store user information across multiple requests,
    - When a user logs in, the server creates a session, assigns it a unique session ID, and sends that ID to the user's browser, typically as a cookie. This session ID allowing it to remember user information without requiring the user to log in again each time.
   - sessions are used to keep a user "logged in" or to store temporary data about them while they use a website.

   code to use Express-session:
    npm install --save express-session

    Whenever same make a request again, user information stored with session, so he don't have to give his login information again





